  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between cholic acid and Cytochrome c oxidase subunit 2, as cholic acid is implicated in targeting multiple subunits of the cytochrome c oxidase complex, including subunits 7A, 7B, and 5A, all of which are located in the mitochondrial matrix. These subunits are known to be involved in the electron transport chain and are critical for cellular respiration. The presence of N-Formylmethionine as a target of these subunits indicates a possible pathway where cholic acid may influence the activity or stability of these proteins. The consistent scores across the three paths (final_score=0.7391) suggest a strong and reliable association, though the exact mechanism by which cholic acid affects these subunits remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a functional link between cholic acid and the cytochrome c oxidase subunit 2, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the biological relevance and specificity of this interaction.",
